👉 Config-driven dynamic CI/CD orchestration

infra-repo/
│
├── cft/
│   ├── base-infra.yaml              # S3, IAM roles, core networking (optional VPC)
│   ├── ssm-parameters.yaml          # initial SSM parameter setup
│   └── bootstrap-lambda-role.yaml   # base execution role for all lambdas
│
├── scripts/
│   ├── seed-ssm.sh                  # initializes environment config in SSM
│   └── validate.sh                  # validates CFN templates locally
│
├── config/
│   └── bootstrap-config.json       # single source for initial setup
│
├── .github/
│   └── workflows/
│       └── bootstrap.yml           # one-time / manual infra deployment
│
├── README.md
└── .gitignore


INFRA-REPO (this repo)
   ↓ creates:
      - S3 buckets
      - IAM roles
      - SSM parameters
   ↓

LAYER-REPO
   ↓ writes:
      /platform/layer/common/latest

SERVICE-REPOS
   ↓ read:
      /platform/dev/s3_bucket
      /platform/layer/common/latest
   ↓ deploy lambdas + CFN stacks








.github/workflows/
  service-deployment-wf.yml          # CI/CD pipeline (GitHub Actions)

infra/
  service-cloudformation-template.yml
  lambda-layer-cloudformation-template.yml

 1️⃣ service-deployment-wf.yml (GitHub Actions)

👉 Orchestrates everything:

build
package
upload to S3
deploy CloudFormation

Think: pipeline logic

2️⃣ service-cloudformation-template.yml

👉 Defines:

Lambda functions
API Gateway
IAM roles

Think: application infrastructure

3️⃣ lambda-layer-cloudformation-template.yml

👉 Defines:

Lambda Layer
Versioning

Think: shared dependency infrastructure

=====================================================================================================================

🧼 Final architecture (what you want)
GitHub Actions
   ↓
[Detect changes]
   ↓
[Deploy Layer Stack]  (only if changed)
   ↓
[Deploy Service Stack]
   ↓
[Update only changed Lambdas]


When this approach shines

This is ideal when:

Multiple stacks (doctor, patient, auth, etc.)
Monorepo structure
You want faster CI/CD and avoid unnecessary deploys



run locallly ./entrypoint.sh dev config/env-config.json cft/doctor.yaml doctor lambdas common-layer
